{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And if you walk with Me קְרִי.</b> Our Rabbis said: עֲרַאי, randomly — that you walk עֲרַאי with the commandments. Menachem explained it as a term of withholding, as in ״הֹקַר רַגְלְךָ״ (Proverbs 25), and as in ״יְקַר רוּחַ״ (ibid. 17). And close to this meaning is the Targum of Onkelos — a term of hardness, that they harden their heart to withhold from drawing near to Me." "<b>Seven as your sins.</b> Seven further punishments, corresponding to the number seven of your sins (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:42.337453943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}